  "problem": "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\" height=\"70px\" align=\"center\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n\n<td height=\"35px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$42$</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\">$18$</td>\n\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
